1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:01,450
(Penny:)I know.

2
00:00:01,450 --> 00:00:05,030
(Todd:)I've always wanted one.

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:07,240
(door slams)

4
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:15,240
(Sheldon:)Well, he's even more cunning
than we thought.

5
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:21,520
(Sheldon:)You know, the joke's on him.

6
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,850
(Sheldon:)Without the certificate of
authenticity,

7
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:26,490
(Sheldon:)that bat'leth is worthless.

8
00:00:26,490 --> 00:00:29,760
(Howard:)Yeah, he walked
right into our trap.

9
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:34,730
(Raj:)Legoland seems like
a hollow dream now.

10
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:38,280
(Leonard(phone rings):)Uh-oh.

11
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:39,990
(Raj:)What's the matter?
Something's wrong.

12
00:00:39,990 --> 00:00:41,640
(Leonard:)I'm not getting any gas.

13
00:00:42,770 --> 00:00:44,810
(rattling)

14
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:51,110
(Leonard:)Anybody know anything about
internal combustion engines?

15
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,080
(Sheldon:)Of course.

16
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:53,580
(Howard:)19th-century technology.
Very basic.

17
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:55,950
(Leonard:)Does anybody know how to fix
an internal combustion engine?

18
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,390
(Leonard:)No. No.
Not a clue.

19
00:00:58,390 --> 00:01:01,520
(Leonard:)Well, we'd better call somebody
to come pick us up.

